1
00:00:18,235 --> 00:00:21,772
You turned down the scholarship
because you needed to work

2
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:23,130
to help your father,

3
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:27,644
who if I'm not mistaken had a heart problem.

4
00:00:27,644 --> 00:00:30,658
Sadly, an intelligent,

5
00:00:30,658 --> 00:00:34,785
hardworking and good student
like you is not in school.

6
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:37,321
I have a proposal for you.

7
00:00:37,321 --> 00:00:41,392
You can still cook for us to help your family

8
00:00:41,392 --> 00:00:48,298
but now you have the option
to study in GU if you want.

9
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:52,035
You might exhaust yourself
and won't have time for yourself.

10
00:00:52,035 --> 00:00:55,222
<i>No, don't worry. I can handle that.</i>

11
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:58,709
<i>Me of all people,
I inherited your good traits.</i>

12
00:00:58,709 --> 00:01:02,846
Just make sure that you can
take care of yourself.

13
00:01:02,846 --> 00:01:07,210
Yes, Mother.
You don't have to worry because I can do this.

14
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:09,054
Isn't Nero okay with you?

15
00:01:09,054 --> 00:01:11,621
He always gives me dagger looks.

16
00:01:11,621 --> 00:01:13,590
He only looks mad, but he's okay with you.

17
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:15,158
As a matter of fact,

18
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,361
he's one of your biggest defenders
here in the mansion.

19
00:01:17,361 --> 00:01:20,864
It's also not a stretch to say
that because of Nero up to now,

20
00:01:20,864 --> 00:01:22,997
you're still the cook for the Ferells.

21
00:01:22,997 --> 00:01:26,602
Sorry, Nero for judging you.

22
00:01:26,602 --> 00:01:29,471
You're okay even if you're a bit weird.

23
00:01:31,274 --> 00:01:34,805
Okay, promise, I will not judge you again.

24
00:01:34,805 --> 00:01:37,508
Well then let me take this opportunity

25
00:01:37,508 --> 00:01:40,884
to tell you
that Don Ferell and I talked already

26
00:01:40,884 --> 00:01:43,787
about sending you to school.

27
00:01:43,787 --> 00:01:46,460
I was planning to talk to you.

28
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:50,093
I just want to let you know
that even though I'll be going to GU,

29
00:01:50,093 --> 00:01:54,131
I will not neglect my work here.

30
00:01:54,131 --> 00:01:59,135
Very good then,
I guess we won't have a problem.

31
00:02:01,738 --> 00:02:04,002
Nero?

32
00:02:04,002 --> 00:02:06,424
He's early.

33
00:02:06,424 --> 00:02:08,025
Where is he going?

34
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,073
Should I confront him tomorrow?

35
00:03:26,073 --> 00:03:30,300
But... it looks like DJ Acapulco is right.

36
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,662
I should give him the time and space...

37
00:03:32,662 --> 00:03:37,634
until he is ready to admit his true feelings.

38
00:03:38,808 --> 00:03:44,074
Wow, feelings, you assume too much Florence.

39
00:03:44,074 --> 00:03:46,376
Who do you think you are, Jennilyn Mercado?

40
00:03:46,376 --> 00:03:49,130
Are you that beautiful for him
to have secret feelings for you?

41
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:50,556
Wow, then.

42
00:03:50,556 --> 00:03:52,190
You think you're...

43
00:03:55,014 --> 00:03:57,116
But what will I wear tomorrow?

44
00:03:59,336 --> 00:04:01,004
A t-shirt?

45
00:04:02,213 --> 00:04:03,747
Flower skirt?

46
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:06,280
This one?

47
00:04:08,198 --> 00:04:09,891
Why are you thinking, Florence?

48
00:04:09,891 --> 00:04:11,835
You're not going on a date with Nero.

49
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:13,200
You'll just go to the farm.

50
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,305
Why are you so concerned about your outfit?

51
00:04:15,305 --> 00:04:18,508
What's happening to you, Florence?

52
00:04:19,555 --> 00:04:26,428
Just be yourself.

53
00:06:43,053 --> 00:06:44,787
Let's play some music.

54
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:48,011
Do you want to sing?

55
00:06:49,818 --> 00:06:51,653
I sing out of tune.

56
00:06:53,296 --> 00:06:55,965
It's not important if you're in tune or not.

57
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,501
What's important is...

58
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,370
you're beautiful.

59
00:07:07,110 --> 00:07:08,644
Let's go.

60
00:07:35,638 --> 00:07:37,974
<i>Do I look okay?</i>

61
00:07:37,974 --> 00:07:40,443
<i>I think I'm overdressed.</i>

62
00:07:56,126 --> 00:07:58,027
What are you doing there? Let's go.

63
00:07:58,027 --> 00:07:59,795
Hurry up.

64
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,434
Coming, sir.

65
00:08:29,526 --> 00:08:31,086
What are you waiting for?

66
00:08:31,086 --> 00:08:32,428
Let's go.

67
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:56,152
Seat belt.

68
00:09:04,427 --> 00:09:05,428
It's so quiet.

69
00:09:05,428 --> 00:09:07,330
Let's play some music.

70
00:09:07,330 --> 00:09:10,533
Don't touch any part of my car.

71
00:09:13,102 --> 00:09:14,971
Okay.

72
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:25,248
So, Nero, how are you?

73
00:09:25,248 --> 00:09:28,852
I was thinking
I'll share some things about myself,

74
00:09:28,852 --> 00:09:31,321
well, you know, we're in the same house

75
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:35,158
so it's better that you know
the people you're with.

76
00:09:35,158 --> 00:09:37,927
So, let's start with your favorite color.

77
00:09:37,927 --> 00:09:41,464
As for me, my favorite color is blue.

78
00:09:41,464 --> 00:09:44,981
I bet you think it's pink
like all the girls out there.

79
00:09:44,981 --> 00:09:46,942
Well, pink is also okay

80
00:09:46,942 --> 00:09:50,169
but the color blue puts me in a better mood.

81
00:09:50,169 --> 00:09:53,067
<i>Oh my, he doesn't even bother
to make small talk.</i>

82
00:09:53,067 --> 00:09:56,803
<i>If you think that I will stop,
well, you're wrong.</i>

83
00:09:57,745 --> 00:09:59,309
Do you like K-Pop?

84
00:09:59,309 --> 00:10:03,019
I think you're into K-Pop.
I'm starting to like K-Pop.

85
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:05,889
I'm excited about
the 4th Generation of K-Pop,

86
00:10:05,889 --> 00:10:09,425
but I will always be a Uaena by heart.

87
00:10:09,425 --> 00:10:11,031
IU will always be my bias,

88
00:10:11,031 --> 00:10:14,318
that's why it's one of my dreams
to travel to Seoul,

89
00:10:14,318 --> 00:10:16,651
and I will hang out in Myeongdong

90
00:10:16,651 --> 00:10:21,070
and I will indulge myself non-stop
in the street food of Korea.

91
00:10:21,070 --> 00:10:22,672
It's so delicious. The best!

92
00:10:22,672 --> 00:10:25,875
Tteokbokki, soondae, mandu!

93
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,026
That's one of my bucket list!

94
00:10:27,026 --> 00:10:29,040
How about you, what's your food trip like?

95
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:31,347
Do you have a favorite food?

96
00:10:34,009 --> 00:10:35,884
Let me guess.

97
00:10:35,884 --> 00:10:40,590
I'm not a judgmental person
but if I were to judge you,

98
00:10:40,590 --> 00:10:45,841
I think your favorite food is Sinigang.

99
00:10:45,841 --> 00:10:48,120
I'm good, right?

100
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:50,300
You're so sour, that's why.

101
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,968
Or grapes?

102
00:10:51,968 --> 00:10:53,036
Are you fond of grapes?

103
00:10:53,036 --> 00:10:54,349
How about bananas?

104
00:10:54,349 --> 00:10:57,590
There's saba, senyorita, lakatan?

105
00:10:57,590 --> 00:10:58,925
Which one is your preference?

106
00:10:58,925 --> 00:11:00,560
Santol? Mangoes?

107
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:02,379
Buko? Buko Pie!

108
00:11:02,379 --> 00:11:04,915
How about tomatoes?

109
00:11:04,915 --> 00:11:09,453
Yup, contrary to the popular belief,
tomatoes are fruits too.

110
00:11:09,453 --> 00:11:12,890
See, your time is not wasted
while hanging out with me

111
00:11:12,890 --> 00:11:16,593
because we're doing
an educational program today.

112
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,139
How about you?

113
00:11:18,139 --> 00:11:20,263
When did you learn how to drive?

114
00:11:21,965 --> 00:11:23,811
Why did we stop?

115
00:11:23,811 --> 00:11:25,535
Are we here already?

116
00:11:32,443 --> 00:11:34,778
Why did you put down the roof?

117
00:11:55,532 --> 00:12:00,904
<i>Relax, Florence, maybe Nero is the shy type,</i>

118
00:12:00,904 --> 00:12:04,958
<i>so find a way
so he can be comfortable with you.</i>

119
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:10,864
<i>So he can tell you the truth
instead of using his doves.</i>

120
00:12:29,896 --> 00:12:31,646
Mama Nida.

121
00:12:31,646 --> 00:12:33,787
- Nero!
- Papa Dante...

122
00:12:33,787 --> 00:12:35,248
- I miss you.
- Nero.

123
00:12:35,248 --> 00:12:37,068
Nero, is that you?

124
00:12:38,542 --> 00:12:41,849
- Papa Dante.
- Son...

125
00:12:41,849 --> 00:12:43,115
How are you?

126
00:12:43,115 --> 00:12:44,715
We miss you too.

127
00:12:44,715 --> 00:12:47,367
We thought you won't visit us here.

128
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:48,552
Is that possible?

129
00:12:48,552 --> 00:12:53,289
And Nero, who are you with?

130
00:12:53,289 --> 00:12:54,823
Me?

131
00:12:56,419 --> 00:13:01,197
Florence Dela Cruz,
I'm the current cook in their mansion.

132
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:05,385
Wow, they hired someone young
to cook in the mansion.

133
00:13:05,385 --> 00:13:07,954
No, they used to hire professionals,

134
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:11,424
but they don't have a choice
because no one wants to cook for them.

135
00:13:11,424 --> 00:13:13,261
Is that so?

136
00:13:13,261 --> 00:13:17,604
I'm Nida by the way,
and this is my husband, Dante.

137
00:13:17,604 --> 00:13:20,483
I already spoke to Don Ferell.

138
00:13:20,483 --> 00:13:24,787
It seems he's so excited about the chopsuey
you're about to cook.

139
00:13:24,787 --> 00:13:26,443
That only means one thing.

140
00:13:26,443 --> 00:13:32,591
Before you can get his trust,
you should be a superb cook.

141
00:13:32,591 --> 00:13:36,666
True, and I'll claim that
because with all the problems on this earth,

142
00:13:36,666 --> 00:13:40,036
we shouldn't add false humility to it.

143
00:13:40,036 --> 00:13:41,782
That's right.

144
00:13:41,782 --> 00:13:44,663
Correct, this kid has a point.

145
00:13:45,650 --> 00:13:48,180
- I miss you so much.
- I miss you too.

146
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:49,274
How are you doing, Son?

147
00:13:49,274 --> 00:13:51,860
I'm doing okay, of course,
just like Papa Dante.

148
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:53,750
See, I told you.

149
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,899
And you believe him?

150
00:13:55,899 --> 00:13:58,367
Of course, his roots are here.

151
00:14:00,353 --> 00:14:02,991
- I don't know about you.
- Yes.

152
00:14:05,561 --> 00:14:08,831
This area, Nero, is where your grandpa
wants to plant strawberries.

153
00:14:08,831 --> 00:14:11,703
The seeds are scheduled to arrive next month.

154
00:14:11,703 --> 00:14:13,836
Why don't you join us in planting them?'

155
00:14:13,836 --> 00:14:15,104
Okay, Papa Dante.

156
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,372
I will tell grandpa.

157
00:14:16,372 --> 00:14:19,542
Hey, you were quick.

158
00:14:19,542 --> 00:14:22,294
This kid is so good.

159
00:14:22,294 --> 00:14:25,091
She's very good at gauging vegetables.

160
00:14:25,091 --> 00:14:30,382
What Ms. Serafica said is right,
this kid is good.

161
00:14:30,382 --> 00:14:32,005
Really?

162
00:14:32,005 --> 00:14:34,123
Let's try.

163
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:38,436
Why did you choose this?

164
00:14:38,436 --> 00:14:40,196
Why this broccoli?

165
00:14:40,196 --> 00:14:43,466
Are you going to test me, Papa Dante?

166
00:14:43,466 --> 00:14:45,741
That's just basic, Papa Dante.
Of course, just based on the color,

167
00:14:45,741 --> 00:14:47,069
you should know right away.

168
00:14:47,069 --> 00:14:49,305
There shouldn't be any brown or yellow spots.

169
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:50,757
When it comes to the stem,

170
00:14:50,757 --> 00:14:53,466
there shouldn't be any patches
of black or white.

171
00:14:53,466 --> 00:14:58,214
And when it comes to the cabbages,
the head must be dense and firm.

172
00:14:58,214 --> 00:15:00,850
And the leaves should be crispy.

173
00:15:00,850 --> 00:15:02,685
With the bell pepper...

174
00:15:02,685 --> 00:15:04,966
You're knowledgeable about vegetables.

175
00:15:04,966 --> 00:15:06,322
How about fruits?

176
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:08,764
When it comes to fruits,
it depends on the type of fruit.

177
00:15:08,764 --> 00:15:11,577
There are different ways to gauge them

178
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:15,137
but usually, with just the color,
you'd be able to know right away.

179
00:15:15,137 --> 00:15:19,268
Another way also is the texture
like the bananas and mangoes.

180
00:15:19,268 --> 00:15:22,955
Just by checking the texture,
you'd know if it's fresh or not.

181
00:15:22,955 --> 00:15:25,623
There are factors that you'd know right away.

182
00:15:25,623 --> 00:15:28,662
You can also check its scent.

183
00:15:28,662 --> 00:15:32,465
Well, both fresh fruits
and not-so-fresh fruits can smell good

184
00:15:32,465 --> 00:15:36,076
but it really smells different
if the fruits are so fresh.

185
00:15:36,076 --> 00:15:38,921
But sometimes,
there are fruits that you can't gauge

186
00:15:38,921 --> 00:15:42,491
just by their outside appearances,
like watermelon and coconut.

187
00:15:42,491 --> 00:15:44,927
Sometimes, no matter how good
they look on the outside,

188
00:15:44,927 --> 00:15:47,196
when you check the inside,
it's not good anymore.

189
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:48,431
- It's no longer fresh.
- That's right.

190
00:15:48,431 --> 00:15:50,016
So what you have to do is

191
00:15:50,016 --> 00:15:53,082
knock on it so you'd know
if it's fresh or not.

192
00:15:53,082 --> 00:15:54,574
So you'd know the truth.

193
00:15:54,574 --> 00:15:58,073
Just like gauging the character of a person.

194
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,454
That's true.

195
00:16:01,811 --> 00:16:03,379
- That's true, right?
- Yes.

196
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:05,665
Because my mother told me, very often,

197
00:16:05,665 --> 00:16:10,245
the outside appearance of a person
is different from their character.

198
00:16:10,245 --> 00:16:13,760
So if you want to know them very well,

199
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:16,258
you should knock on their hearts.

200
00:16:19,328 --> 00:16:20,396
Cheers?

201
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:21,997
Cheers.

202
00:16:24,166 --> 00:16:27,503
Dad, is this one of your life lessons?

203
00:16:27,503 --> 00:16:29,449
How to knock at someone's heart?

204
00:16:29,449 --> 00:16:30,983
Just like this?

205
00:16:33,609 --> 00:16:34,744
Go ahead, son,

206
00:16:34,744 --> 00:16:39,879
laugh at me but someday,
the time will come when you will say,

207
00:16:39,879 --> 00:16:42,054
"Dad is right".

208
00:16:42,054 --> 00:16:44,420
Because believe it or not...

209
00:16:45,609 --> 00:16:50,325
you'll only know a person
if you know what's inside of them.

210
00:16:53,366 --> 00:16:54,449
- Dad,
- It's good.

211
00:16:54,449 --> 00:16:57,133
I believe in what you're saying.

212
00:16:57,133 --> 00:17:01,003
My only question is
how do you knock on someone's heart?

213
00:17:05,741 --> 00:17:07,777
That's correct.

214
00:17:10,066 --> 00:17:12,372
Florence, my child.

215
00:17:12,372 --> 00:17:14,700
Let me ask you.

216
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:21,159
What if the person whose heart
you're knocking to

217
00:17:21,159 --> 00:17:25,878
refuses to let you in his life?

218
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:27,763
That's not possible.

219
00:17:27,763 --> 00:17:30,566
What if he really refused to let you in?

220
00:17:31,784 --> 00:17:33,219
I will just keep on knocking...

221
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:36,777
Knock, knock, knock, until he opens the door.

222
00:17:36,777 --> 00:17:39,747
If he doesn't want to open the door,
I'll destroy it.

223
00:17:39,747 --> 00:17:41,786
If I need to sneak into the sidelines

224
00:17:41,786 --> 00:17:45,591
or peep out the window so he'd let me in,
I'll do it.

225
00:17:45,591 --> 00:17:48,351
If I need to shout, I will shout.

226
00:17:48,351 --> 00:17:53,222
Hey, let me in your heart!

227
00:17:53,222 --> 00:17:56,325
- Hey, let her in your heart!
- Hey, let me in your heart!

228
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:59,462
Let me in for the kind of beauty
you're not expecting,

229
00:17:59,462 --> 00:18:01,163
just like me.

230
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,398
I'm sure he'll let you in.

231
00:18:02,398 --> 00:18:03,733
- Really?
- Yes.

232
00:18:03,733 --> 00:18:06,668
- Let her in your heart!
- Let me in you heart!

233
00:18:09,638 --> 00:18:13,575
I don't know if he will let you in with that.

234
00:18:39,911 --> 00:18:41,850
What's his problem?

235
00:18:46,804 --> 00:18:48,015
Cheers?

236
00:18:48,015 --> 00:18:49,845
Cheers.

237
00:18:51,725 --> 00:18:55,151
Dad, is this one of your life lessons?

238
00:18:55,151 --> 00:18:56,892
How to knock at someone's heart?

239
00:18:56,892 --> 00:18:58,360
Just like this?

240
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,560
<i>Go ahead, son, laugh at me,</i>

241
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:07,454
but someday the time will come
when you will say,

242
00:19:07,454 --> 00:19:09,465
"Dad is right".

243
00:19:09,465 --> 00:19:12,034
Because believe it or not...

244
00:19:12,886 --> 00:19:17,690
you'll only know a person
if you know what's inside of them.

245
00:19:20,643 --> 00:19:21,983
- Dad,
- It's good.

246
00:19:21,983 --> 00:19:24,647
I believe in what you're saying.

247
00:19:24,647 --> 00:19:28,483
My only question is
how do you knock on someone's heart?

248
00:19:36,749 --> 00:19:40,354
Know the story of their life.

249
00:19:40,354 --> 00:19:45,578
Listen without mocking or judgment.

250
00:19:45,578 --> 00:19:49,504
And put yourself in their situation.

251
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:59,520
Okay, but Dad,

252
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:03,368
there won't come a time
when someone will knock at my heart,

253
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:06,165
because I will be the one
to knock at someone else's heart

254
00:20:06,165 --> 00:20:08,324
when I start courting.

255
00:20:08,324 --> 00:20:10,443
You're full of foolishness.

256
00:20:10,443 --> 00:20:14,448
But Dad, was it you
who knocked at Mom's heart?

257
00:20:17,745 --> 00:20:20,769
With your mom, it's the opposite.

258
00:20:20,769 --> 00:20:24,173
It was her who first knocked at my heart.

259
00:20:24,173 --> 00:20:25,541
- Really?
- Yes.

260
00:20:25,541 --> 00:20:26,876
Wow.

261
00:20:26,876 --> 00:20:28,550
Mom is aggressive.

262
00:20:28,550 --> 00:20:30,212
She made the first move.

263
00:20:30,212 --> 00:20:33,333
Even the second and third moves.

264
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:35,969
Wait, she might hear me.

265
00:20:38,678 --> 00:20:40,924
But you know, son,

266
00:20:40,924 --> 00:20:46,455
I wish the time would never come

267
00:20:46,455 --> 00:20:50,265
when you'd feel that something
is lacking in your life.

268
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:54,353
But when that day comes...

269
00:20:54,353 --> 00:20:59,706
I hope you'll meet someone
who will knock on your heart.

270
00:20:59,706 --> 00:21:02,778
That's my prayer.

271
00:21:03,763 --> 00:21:06,999
And so, let her in.

272
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:12,810
So she would know the real you.

273
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:19,027
And for you to realize that
nothing is lacking with you.

274
00:21:20,156 --> 00:21:25,794
There's a big space in the heart to love.

275
00:21:30,506 --> 00:21:32,664
Hand me one more.

276
00:21:32,664 --> 00:21:34,543
This is your third.

277
00:21:45,074 --> 00:21:46,808
Rambutan.

278
00:21:48,691 --> 00:21:50,425
What?

279
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:56,807
You're asking me
what's my favorite fruit, right?

280
00:21:58,767 --> 00:22:00,452
It's rambutan.

281
00:22:14,116 --> 00:22:16,017
My favorite...

282
00:22:18,387 --> 00:22:22,404
because it tastes like a kiss.

283
00:22:30,332 --> 00:22:37,506
Does rambutan taste like a kiss?

284
00:22:37,506 --> 00:22:39,541
Do you want to taste...

285
00:22:53,730 --> 00:22:55,798
the rambutan?

286
00:23:03,918 --> 00:23:06,135
The rambutan tastes sweet.

287
00:23:08,307 --> 00:23:10,215
What's with you, Florencia?

288
00:23:10,215 --> 00:23:12,777
What kind of imagination is that?

289
00:23:12,777 --> 00:23:17,049
Nero just told you his favorite fruit,
and now you had a dream like that?

290
00:23:39,925 --> 00:23:43,428
What's the taste of the kiss of the rambutan?

291
00:23:45,136 --> 00:23:48,191
Most likely it tastes like rambutan, but...

292
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:51,489
is it sweeter?

293
00:23:51,489 --> 00:23:53,682
It depends on the rambutan.

294
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:55,717
Son of the rambutan!

295
00:23:56,418 --> 00:23:58,599
- Grandpa Garp?
- Yes.

296
00:23:59,747 --> 00:24:01,942
Why are you here?

297
00:24:01,942 --> 00:24:04,426
I'm eating leftover chopsuey. It's delicious.

298
00:24:04,426 --> 00:24:06,862
Just like I imagined.

299
00:24:08,106 --> 00:24:12,333
Oh thanks, by the way,
you granted my request.

300
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:16,138
You're welcome, but Grandpa Garp...

301
00:24:16,138 --> 00:24:19,475
why are you eating in the dark?

302
00:24:19,475 --> 00:24:20,776
I can't find the switch.

303
00:24:20,776 --> 00:24:22,578
I don't want to disturb you.

304
00:24:22,578 --> 00:24:25,114
That's okay. The switch is over there.

305
00:24:25,114 --> 00:24:29,358
Next time you get hungry around this time,
just call me.

306
00:24:29,358 --> 00:24:30,920
Duly noted.

307
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,350
I also have one request.

308
00:24:32,350 --> 00:24:34,606
Can you please make me a cup of coffee?

309
00:24:34,606 --> 00:24:40,459
Sure, but is it okay with you
if I make a Cafe-ala-Florencia for you?

310
00:24:40,459 --> 00:24:42,223
Yeah, sure.

311
00:24:42,223 --> 00:24:43,932
What's that?

312
00:24:53,907 --> 00:24:56,042
I'm sorry, Dad.

313
00:24:57,312 --> 00:24:59,543
I miss you so much.

314
00:25:04,753 --> 00:25:06,821
I miss you.

315
00:25:22,838 --> 00:25:24,406
By the way...

316
00:25:24,406 --> 00:25:27,042
how was your trip to the farm?

317
00:25:27,042 --> 00:25:28,643
How's Nero?

318
00:25:32,181 --> 00:25:36,592
With the 100 questions I asked him,

319
00:25:36,592 --> 00:25:40,756
he answered one question,
so, it's not so bad.

320
00:25:40,756 --> 00:25:43,859
And somehow he spoke.

321
00:25:43,859 --> 00:25:45,561
He's really like that.

322
00:25:45,561 --> 00:25:49,965
You know, with this trip,
I was hoping he would socialize with you.

323
00:25:51,233 --> 00:25:57,572
Well, he's okay with Mr. Dante and Ms. Nida,
but he was ignoring me a bit.

324
00:25:59,141 --> 00:26:02,244
By the way, I have a question if it's okay.

325
00:26:02,244 --> 00:26:03,678
Okay, sure.

326
00:26:04,379 --> 00:26:06,548
Did something happen to Nero?

327
00:26:06,548 --> 00:26:08,750
Why did he become like that?

328
00:26:08,750 --> 00:26:12,855
You know, Nero only became like that
ever since his father died.

329
00:26:12,855 --> 00:26:16,838
I'm sorry I made you remember
that painful memory.

330
00:26:16,838 --> 00:26:19,694
No, don't be sorry.
After all, it's been three years.

331
00:26:21,463 --> 00:26:25,434
My son did not enjoy a luxurious life.

332
00:26:25,434 --> 00:26:29,794
He and his wife, Eliza,
were doctors to the barrios.

333
00:26:29,794 --> 00:26:32,154
That's where they formed their family...

334
00:26:32,154 --> 00:26:35,254
in Barrio Masagana, in Santa Rita.

335
00:26:35,254 --> 00:26:39,414
Nero grew up in the province,
so he's more of a provincial guy.

336
00:26:42,638 --> 00:26:45,040
Nero loves his father so much.

337
00:26:49,525 --> 00:26:51,018
You take this once a day.

338
00:26:51,018 --> 00:26:52,807
And this too, okay?

339
00:26:52,807 --> 00:26:53,829
Here.

340
00:26:53,829 --> 00:26:55,397
Thank you.

341
00:27:00,502 --> 00:27:02,704
Are you okay, son?

342
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:04,205
I want to go home now.

343
00:27:06,141 --> 00:27:07,342
There are a few patients left.

344
00:27:07,342 --> 00:27:09,377
Your mom and I won't be long.

345
00:27:10,412 --> 00:27:12,614
I thought we'll just be here
for a short time.

346
00:27:14,750 --> 00:27:18,079
I promised Troy that we'll line up
for the opening of Infinity Wars.

347
00:27:18,079 --> 00:27:21,248
I shouldn't have joined you
if I knew I'd be stuck here.

348
00:27:33,806 --> 00:27:35,176
Nero!

349
00:27:36,980 --> 00:27:39,167
Stop being unreasonable.

350
00:27:39,167 --> 00:27:42,035
Are you having an attack of selfishness?

351
00:27:42,035 --> 00:27:45,519
Me and your dad are doing
something more important here

352
00:27:45,519 --> 00:27:46,972
than what you want.

353
00:27:46,972 --> 00:27:50,933
You better grow up, and while you're at it,

354
00:27:50,933 --> 00:27:53,138
check your privileges as well.

355
00:27:53,138 --> 00:27:55,761
Stop acting like the world
is revolving around you

356
00:27:55,761 --> 00:27:58,354
and start being like your dad!

357
00:27:58,354 --> 00:28:01,313
He's using his position to help others.

358
00:28:01,313 --> 00:28:04,729
You're turning out to be
a big disappointment!

359
00:28:04,729 --> 00:28:06,864
You're an embarrassment!

360
00:28:10,572 --> 00:28:12,016
Are you really not feeling well?

361
00:28:12,016 --> 00:28:13,241
No.

362
00:28:15,374 --> 00:28:17,188
If you were bored earlier, Nero,

363
00:28:17,188 --> 00:28:21,530
you should've just told us
instead of making up excuses.

364
00:28:22,421 --> 00:28:24,219
I'm sorry, Dad.

365
00:28:24,219 --> 00:28:26,277
I appreciate what you're doing,

366
00:28:26,277 --> 00:28:30,125
but it's Tristan's birthday,
and there's a big party in the mansion.

367
00:28:32,235 --> 00:28:36,232
Like what I said, son,
you should've just told me.

368
00:28:36,232 --> 00:28:39,435
I'll let you go to Tristan's party.

369
00:28:39,435 --> 00:28:41,437
You will, Dad, but how about Mom?

370
00:28:42,738 --> 00:28:45,107
She is expecting me to be like you,

371
00:28:45,107 --> 00:28:47,210
that's why I need to be on your tail always.

372
00:28:47,210 --> 00:28:49,008
The last time I asked permission from her,

373
00:28:49,008 --> 00:28:51,280
she made me feel that
I was just wasting my time.

374
00:28:51,280 --> 00:28:53,082
Instead of me enjoying time with my friends,

375
00:28:53,082 --> 00:28:54,884
I should just help others

376
00:28:54,884 --> 00:28:57,620
and join you in your medical missions.

377
00:28:57,620 --> 00:28:59,322
Dad, I'm proud of what you're doing,

378
00:28:59,322 --> 00:29:02,291
but sometimes,
I just want to be a normal teenager.

379
00:29:02,291 --> 00:29:05,661
To be a Ferell and enjoy with my cousins
with grandpa.

380
00:29:06,631 --> 00:29:09,198
Don't worry, I'll talk to your mom.

381
00:29:09,198 --> 00:29:13,870
Maybe it's better if we don't bring you along
to our activities.

382
00:29:13,870 --> 00:29:17,656
You can still join us
if you feel like joining us...

383
00:29:17,656 --> 00:29:20,360
but you don't have to go with me and your mom

384
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:23,579
to our outreach programs
and medical missions.

385
00:29:24,347 --> 00:29:25,805
Dad!

386
00:29:27,350 --> 00:29:31,254
Eliza, don't blame Nero for what happened.

387
00:29:31,254 --> 00:29:33,805
I need some time alone, Papa.

388
00:29:33,805 --> 00:29:39,618
I need time to process all these things
that are happening to me.

389
00:29:39,618 --> 00:29:41,774
I hope you understand.

390
00:29:43,649 --> 00:29:47,019
Well, if that's what you want,
I won't stop you.

391
00:29:47,019 --> 00:29:49,421
Please take care of Nero.

392
00:29:49,421 --> 00:29:53,239
I'll come back once I'm ready to face him.

393
00:30:18,708 --> 00:30:21,654
I failed, Florence.

394
00:30:21,654 --> 00:30:23,688
I failed to heal my grandson.

395
00:30:24,556 --> 00:30:26,125
This is all my fault.

396
00:30:26,125 --> 00:30:28,393
I should've been a better grandpa.

397
00:30:32,031 --> 00:30:34,400
You know what, Grandpa Garp?

398
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:37,773
One of the things my mother taught me is...

399
00:30:37,773 --> 00:30:42,141
that the most powerful cure for pain is time,

400
00:30:42,141 --> 00:30:44,943
because if the days become a month,

401
00:30:44,943 --> 00:30:49,615
and months turn into years,
no matter how deep,

402
00:30:49,615 --> 00:30:52,717
the pain and wounds will heal.

403
00:30:55,454 --> 00:30:58,157
You know, your mother is right.

404
00:30:58,157 --> 00:31:00,693
And thank you so much, Florence.

405
00:31:00,693 --> 00:31:04,930
You reminded me not to lose hope.

406
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:10,013
More chopsuey?

407
00:31:16,127 --> 00:31:18,062
Florence, what's for breakfast?

408
00:31:18,693 --> 00:31:20,994
There, it's right in front of you.
It will bite you.

409
00:31:20,994 --> 00:31:22,381
Don't you have eyes?

410
00:31:22,381 --> 00:31:24,316
You're so grouchy this early.

411
00:31:24,316 --> 00:31:26,385
Happy morning, Troy and Owen.

412
00:31:26,385 --> 00:31:28,919
I made you some juice,
coffee, or hot chocolate.

413
00:31:28,919 --> 00:31:30,138
What do you want to drink?

414
00:31:30,138 --> 00:31:32,341
We're okay with the orange juice.
Thank you, Florence.

415
00:31:32,341 --> 00:31:36,462
- Thank you.
- Wait, why is there favoritism here?

416
00:31:36,462 --> 00:31:37,896
With Troy and Owen, you're sweet,

417
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:39,932
- but to Tristan and me, you're grouchy.
- That's true.

418
00:31:39,932 --> 00:31:41,066
Maybe you're not nice.

419
00:31:41,066 --> 00:31:42,067
Do we have to be nice?

420
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:43,838
I pity you.

421
00:31:43,838 --> 00:31:45,303
What's your problem?

422
00:31:45,303 --> 00:31:47,332
Hey, let me just flex that these two guys

423
00:31:47,332 --> 00:31:49,575
are the sweetest to me in the mansion so...

424
00:31:49,575 --> 00:31:50,676
We're sweet too.

425
00:31:50,676 --> 00:31:51,844
In your face.

426
00:31:51,844 --> 00:31:53,445
Let's go and eat.

427
00:31:55,907 --> 00:31:57,158
Attack!

428
00:32:00,876 --> 00:32:02,464
Where is Nero?

429
00:32:03,322 --> 00:32:05,891
He's having an attack of mood swings.

430
00:32:05,891 --> 00:32:07,993
Is he a weirdo again for today?

431
00:32:08,956 --> 00:32:10,791
It's actually his dad's birthday...

432
00:32:11,433 --> 00:32:14,266
so we should be extra careful with him today.

433
00:32:14,266 --> 00:32:17,803
Or better yet, no one should go near him.

434
00:32:17,803 --> 00:32:19,471
Let him be by himself.

435
00:32:33,819 --> 00:32:36,722
Florence, you called. Do you have a problem?

436
00:32:36,722 --> 00:32:37,923
What's with you?

437
00:32:37,923 --> 00:32:39,685
She just called and you're thinking
there's a problem right away.

438
00:32:39,685 --> 00:32:41,994
Maybe she's just checking on us.

439
00:32:41,994 --> 00:32:47,166
<i>Father, I don't always call
because I have a problem.</i>

440
00:32:47,166 --> 00:32:50,569
But now, Father, I do have a small problem.

441
00:32:50,569 --> 00:32:52,671
Just a small one.

442
00:32:52,671 --> 00:32:54,807
Did someone insult you?

443
00:32:54,807 --> 00:32:55,807
Are you feeling down?

444
00:32:55,807 --> 00:32:58,449
Do you have an existential crisis
that you're going through?

445
00:32:58,449 --> 00:33:00,230
Father is overreacting.

446
00:33:00,230 --> 00:33:01,540
I'm having problems

447
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:05,750
because there's a fruit that I need
but it's not in season.

448
00:33:07,086 --> 00:33:08,605
What's that?

449
00:33:16,628 --> 00:33:18,564
This house is so far.

450
00:33:18,564 --> 00:33:20,286
What is this house?

451
00:33:20,286 --> 00:33:21,699
My God.

452
00:33:22,310 --> 00:33:24,394
I think I'll have a heart attack.

453
00:33:25,704 --> 00:33:27,939
I'm feeling dizzy...

454
00:33:27,939 --> 00:33:30,129
- Dizzy.
- It feels like I lost weight.

455
00:33:30,129 --> 00:33:32,504
I have a feeling I became sexy.

456
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:51,246
Hey, you look as if
you really saw someone sexy.

457
00:33:52,833 --> 00:33:56,513
Look at you. You're so naughty. Naughty...

458
00:33:56,513 --> 00:33:58,203
Mother! Father!

459
00:33:58,203 --> 00:33:59,104
- Dear!
- Oh, Florence!

460
00:33:59,104 --> 00:34:00,305
Father!

461
00:34:01,606 --> 00:34:02,774
I missed you.

462
00:34:02,774 --> 00:34:04,109
Hey, you look thin.

463
00:34:04,109 --> 00:34:06,678
Wait, why are you out of your room
with incomplete clothing?

464
00:34:06,678 --> 00:34:08,605
Father, that's how things are here.

465
00:34:08,605 --> 00:34:10,716
But Father, you look handsome.

466
00:34:10,716 --> 00:34:12,451
You know Mother, if I didn't know Father,

467
00:34:12,451 --> 00:34:14,753
I would say having a heart disease
suits him well.

468
00:34:14,753 --> 00:34:16,324
Hey, Florencia!

469
00:34:17,022 --> 00:34:19,057
I'm sorry, Mother. It's just a joke.

470
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:22,094
Your mother doesn't really
have a sense of humor.

471
00:34:22,094 --> 00:34:25,097
You shouldn't be making a joke
about heart disease.

472
00:34:25,097 --> 00:34:26,865
Father, Mother is right.

473
00:34:26,865 --> 00:34:29,301
Bad joke... bad joke, Florencia!

474
00:34:29,301 --> 00:34:31,555
I'm sorry, Mother. I just miss you,

475
00:34:31,555 --> 00:34:33,672
and I'm happy that I saw you again.

476
00:34:33,672 --> 00:34:35,540
I also miss you, Florence.

477
00:34:35,540 --> 00:34:38,143
We miss you so much at home.

478
00:34:38,844 --> 00:34:40,078
If you only know.

479
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:44,116
I always catch your mother
staring at your picture, crying.

480
00:34:44,116 --> 00:34:45,350
You're something else.

481
00:34:45,350 --> 00:34:48,286
Anyway, Florence,
here's the thing you asked us to buy.

482
00:34:49,688 --> 00:34:51,590
Is that enough?

483
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:54,760
This is perfect, Mother.

484
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:56,928
Thank you, Mother.

485
00:34:57,729 --> 00:34:59,631
Mother, why don't you come in first?

486
00:34:59,631 --> 00:35:01,333
No, thank you.

487
00:35:01,333 --> 00:35:03,702
Are you sure? Even for a while?

488
00:35:03,702 --> 00:35:04,803
I still have to make her walk.

489
00:35:04,803 --> 00:35:06,349
Maybe there's a chance she can become sexy.

490
00:35:06,349 --> 00:35:08,206
- Hey, you!
- Mother is sexy.

491
00:35:08,206 --> 00:35:11,171
You better go in because you might get sick.

492
00:35:11,171 --> 00:35:13,145
- Okay. Take care.
- You better dress properly.

493
00:35:13,145 --> 00:35:14,146
Wear something...

494
00:35:14,146 --> 00:35:16,548
- Take care.
- Okay, take care, my child.

495
00:35:16,548 --> 00:35:18,116
- I love you, Florence.
- I love you, Mother, Father!

496
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,240
I love you. Love you, Florence!

497
00:35:32,276 --> 00:35:35,011
Operation Rambutan commences.

498
00:35:36,377 --> 00:35:38,074
You know what?

499
00:35:38,074 --> 00:35:40,339
You're so beautiful.

500
00:35:40,339 --> 00:35:44,076
You look like Gretchen Barretto so much.

501
00:35:44,076 --> 00:35:49,010
Especially with this side view
and in the dark.

502
00:35:51,283 --> 00:35:52,484
Thank you.

503
00:35:52,484 --> 00:35:54,720
I'll take that as a compliment.

504
00:35:54,720 --> 00:35:56,755
What's with you?

505
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:59,157
Don't take it as a compliment.

506
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:03,661
Take it as a supplement
so that it's more nutritious.

507
00:36:07,006 --> 00:36:08,266
You're something else.

508
00:36:08,266 --> 00:36:10,134
You always make me laugh.

509
00:36:15,626 --> 00:36:16,731
Why?

510
00:36:17,642 --> 00:36:19,778
Can you sense danger?

511
00:36:19,778 --> 00:36:21,458
It seems there's a different smell.

512
00:36:24,816 --> 00:36:26,184
Hey.

513
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:29,388
Serafica, I took a bath.

514
00:36:29,388 --> 00:36:31,590
And after I took a bath,

515
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:36,528
I scrubbed using fabric conditioner
with perfume collection.

516
00:36:36,528 --> 00:36:38,130
No, there's really a different scent.

517
00:36:38,130 --> 00:36:40,165
I can't smell anything.

518
00:36:40,165 --> 00:36:43,368
I'm sure there's a new scent.

519
00:36:43,368 --> 00:36:46,304
It's faint smell and it seems like...

520
00:36:46,304 --> 00:36:48,440
there's something different in the kitchen.

521
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:51,127
I should know because I spent years here,

522
00:36:51,127 --> 00:36:54,713
that's why I know
if there's a new scent or what.

523
00:36:54,713 --> 00:36:58,316
Oh, I know it already.

524
00:36:58,316 --> 00:37:01,253
Maybe you can smell...

525
00:37:01,253 --> 00:37:05,036
the warmth of my love.

526
00:37:06,491 --> 00:37:08,239
I agree.

527
00:37:08,239 --> 00:37:09,461
The scent is so strong,

528
00:37:09,461 --> 00:37:11,830
and you have a good and genuine character.

529
00:37:11,830 --> 00:37:13,098
Really?

530
00:37:13,098 --> 00:37:14,833
Serafica?

531
00:37:14,833 --> 00:37:17,202
Let's leave this place now.

532
00:37:17,202 --> 00:37:25,053
We might get the kitchen dirty,
with our burning feelings.

533
00:37:26,778 --> 00:37:28,413
I'll go with you.

534
00:37:28,413 --> 00:37:29,948
Let's go.

535
00:37:29,948 --> 00:37:32,317
You're something else. Stop it!

536
00:38:41,987 --> 00:38:43,321
Where's the switch?

537
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:44,458
Here.

538
00:38:46,591 --> 00:38:48,091
Why is there none?

539
00:39:00,427 --> 00:39:02,174
Why is it here?

540
00:39:02,174 --> 00:39:04,642
Switch at the back? Really?

541
00:39:12,851 --> 00:39:14,919
It seems it's going to explode.

542
00:39:19,324 --> 00:39:21,303
In fairness.

543
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:27,699
Hey you, don't be noisy.

544
00:39:27,699 --> 00:39:29,880
You act as if I'm a stranger to you

545
00:39:29,880 --> 00:39:33,938
though you go to me every morning
to send messages.

546
00:39:34,806 --> 00:39:38,676
You're surprised? I know your boss' secret.

547
00:39:41,112 --> 00:39:42,681
Maybe he thinks,

548
00:39:42,681 --> 00:39:47,219
he's the only one capable of
sending those secret messages.

549
00:39:47,219 --> 00:39:49,625
If he's sending secret messages,

550
00:39:49,625 --> 00:39:52,890
then I have secret fruit, rambutan.

551
00:40:19,784 --> 00:40:23,054
You look handsome up front, Mr. Ferell.

552
00:40:24,189 --> 00:40:26,824
Nero got his looks from you.

553
00:40:28,026 --> 00:40:32,597
But you know, you raised Nero very well.

554
00:40:32,597 --> 00:40:34,398
He's a good person.

555
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,769
He's been secretly kind to me.

556
00:40:37,769 --> 00:40:41,172
I thought at first he was so grouchy to me.

557
00:40:42,407 --> 00:40:45,745
Don't touch any part of my car.

558
00:40:49,681 --> 00:40:51,326
It turns out he's not.

559
00:40:52,117 --> 00:40:55,419
He is hurting because of your passing.

560
00:40:58,423 --> 00:41:02,866
I have a little favor to ask you.

561
00:41:03,725 --> 00:41:07,522
Can you visit Nero?

562
00:41:07,522 --> 00:41:11,503
But don't scare him off.

563
00:41:11,503 --> 00:41:22,314
Just visit him in his dreams,
and then tell him that...

564
00:41:23,248 --> 00:41:26,584
there are people who care for him.

565
00:41:26,584 --> 00:41:33,574
Especially Grandpa Garp and me too,
even slightly...

566
00:41:35,226 --> 00:41:37,631
I care for Nero.

567
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:42,500
See, I have some rambutan for you.

568
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:44,866
I hope Nero will like it.

569
00:41:46,249 --> 00:41:47,572
I already said a lot of things.

570
00:41:47,572 --> 00:41:48,602
I'll go ahead.

571
00:41:48,602 --> 00:41:52,888
He shouldn't catch me here, so it's a secret.

572
00:41:52,888 --> 00:41:54,350
I'll go ahead.

573
00:42:19,371 --> 00:42:20,697
The doves.

574
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:25,410
Hey, hey, get out! Get out of there.

575
00:42:25,410 --> 00:42:27,309
This way.

576
00:42:27,309 --> 00:42:30,615
Come here. Hurry. Get out.

577
00:42:30,615 --> 00:42:33,517
They don't want to go out. Go, go, go.

578
00:42:34,456 --> 00:42:36,521
Hey! There. Are there any doves left?

579
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:39,423
You two get out. Let's go.

580
00:42:42,947 --> 00:42:44,169
Let's go.

581
00:42:46,431 --> 00:42:47,685
The picture.

582
00:43:16,027 --> 00:43:17,829
Hurry! The fire is getting bigger!

583
00:43:17,829 --> 00:43:19,430
Hurry!

584
00:43:21,099 --> 00:43:23,501
- Call the firemen!
- Move back!

585
00:43:23,501 --> 00:43:24,803
Move back!

586
00:43:24,803 --> 00:43:27,305
- Water, water!
- It's getting near.

587
00:43:27,305 --> 00:43:28,807
- Water!
- It's getting near!

588
00:43:28,807 --> 00:43:30,575
Did anyone bring a phone?

589
00:43:30,575 --> 00:43:32,777
- We need a phone!
- Call the fire department!

590
00:43:32,777 --> 00:43:33,983
Move away!

591
00:43:35,980 --> 00:43:37,749
- There's no more water!
- Did anyone bring a phone?

592
00:43:37,749 --> 00:43:39,050
What happened to my cabin?

593
00:43:39,050 --> 00:43:40,452
- Hey!
- Nero, Nero!

594
00:43:40,452 --> 00:43:42,353
- My things! Let go of me!
- Hey! Nero, Nero, Nero!

595
00:43:42,353 --> 00:43:43,555
My things!

596
00:43:43,555 --> 00:43:45,924
- There's nothing we can do.
- You don't understand.

597
00:43:45,924 --> 00:43:47,525
- My things are important to me!
- Keep him away!

598
00:43:47,525 --> 00:43:49,360
My cabin!

599
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:51,796
- It's dangerous!
- Wait! My things!

600
00:43:51,796 --> 00:43:53,331
- My things! Let go of me!
- Stop it, Nero!

601
00:43:53,331 --> 00:43:54,332
Wait.

602
00:43:54,332 --> 00:43:57,469
You don't understand! I need my things!

603
00:43:57,469 --> 00:43:59,170
It's dangerous!

604
00:43:59,170 --> 00:44:00,939
- Stop it, Nero!
- Nero, that's enough!

605
00:44:00,939 --> 00:44:03,007
- That's enough!
- Stop it!

606
00:44:13,685 --> 00:44:15,075
That's enough!

607
00:44:16,821 --> 00:44:18,590
Why do you have this?

608
00:44:18,590 --> 00:44:20,257
What are you doing here?

609
00:44:22,627 --> 00:44:24,786
What are you doing here?

610
00:44:27,265 --> 00:44:28,533
I'm sorry.

611
00:44:28,533 --> 00:44:30,101
I didn't mean it.

612
00:44:30,101 --> 00:44:32,370
All of a sudden, there was a fire.

613
00:44:32,370 --> 00:44:35,106
Nero... just calm down.

614
00:44:35,106 --> 00:44:36,774
Let's find out first what happened.

615
00:44:36,774 --> 00:44:38,809
Maybe all of this was just an accident.

616
00:44:39,744 --> 00:44:43,314
This woman destroyed a place
that's very important to me.

617
00:44:43,314 --> 00:44:45,049
How can I calm down?

618
00:44:45,049 --> 00:44:47,485
Tell me how can I calm down?

619
00:44:47,485 --> 00:44:49,521
I'm sure Florence didn't mean to do this.

620
00:44:49,521 --> 00:44:52,357
Hey Owen, stop it first.
It's not the time to take sides.

621
00:44:52,357 --> 00:44:54,959
What Owen is saying is
don't jump to conclusions.

622
00:44:54,959 --> 00:44:57,562
Maybe Florence has an explanation for this.

623
00:44:57,562 --> 00:44:58,596
You too.

624
00:44:58,596 --> 00:45:03,801
Stop it! Everyone should stop,
and please, everyone, inside!

625
00:45:04,702 --> 00:45:06,237
Do you think Nero will forgive her?

626
00:45:06,237 --> 00:45:09,274
I don't think so, because knowing Nero,

627
00:45:09,274 --> 00:45:11,743
he's one of the toughest people that I know.

628
00:45:11,743 --> 00:45:14,913
Knowing Florence,
she can be quite persuasive.

629
00:45:14,913 --> 00:45:16,214
Let's make a bet.

630
00:45:16,214 --> 00:45:17,517
Owen and I will make a bet.

631
00:45:17,518 --> 00:45:18,652
Game.

632
00:45:22,200 --> 00:45:24,400
[Forgiveness is an expensive gift.
Not everyone deserves it.]

633
00:45:28,934 --> 00:45:30,002
Nero?

634
00:45:30,002 --> 00:45:32,270
You owe me three P's.

635
00:45:32,270 --> 00:45:34,673
Human Development Program of the government?

636
00:45:34,673 --> 00:45:38,574
I meant, you owe me three favors.

637
00:45:38,575 --> 00:45:40,701
What kind of favor?

638
00:45:40,701 --> 00:45:42,770
Any.

639
00:45:42,770 --> 00:45:44,430
As in any favor?

640
00:45:44,430 --> 00:45:45,790
Yes.
